WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.920
Anything you want,
you can get it.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.200
We have people from
all cultural background.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.240
We have Africans.
We have Jamaican.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.360
We have persons
from all over.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.440
Ghana, Nigeria,
Jamaica, Caribbean,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.080
you know, everywhere.
You get it here.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.560
You can choose
whatever you like.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.560
Literally everything.
If you want a rug,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.480
if you want curtains,
if you want food,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.520
if you want fashion...

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.120
Anything
you can actually think about,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.520
we've got it here.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.840
I work in Edmonton Green
Shopping Centre.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.360
I have been working
in this street market,

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.760
it's coming to one year
this month.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.320
I'm a proud trader

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.160
in the Edmonton Green
Shopping Centre.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.440
I been working here
almost a year now.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.640
I've been working
north Edmonton Market

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.160
for about 18, 20 years.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.480
It's a beautiful market.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.160
It's a community.
It's a friendly one.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.800
Young people, fun people,
elderly people.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.400
My name is Ameya John-Lewis.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.240
I sell African prints, lace,

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.720
and I'm a tailor. I combine
everything together.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.520
The name of my shop is

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.240
Ameya World
Professional Style.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.520
It's called Ameya World
because it's my world.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.200
Why I choose that name?
I don't know.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.040
It's my godfather
that chooses the name for me

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.520
because it's my real
native name.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:29.680
My birth name.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.320
I started making clothes
when I was young

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.240
because I grew up
seeing my mummy sewing

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.360
and every day I said,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.200
"One day,
I'm going to be sewing."

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.320
So, when I grew up

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.680
I just fell in love with it
straight away.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.200
Because
I love to do something,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.720
I would like to be creative.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.640
More or less,
I have self-taught passion.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.000
I have passion
for what I do.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.440
I'm from Nigeria.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.120
Nigerian culture
is very beautiful.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.880
We are very colourful

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.680
in terms of our party
and dressing up.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.960
When I design for someone,

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.200
I sew for customer
and they like it.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.160
They come back
and give me the review.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.000
They're: "Ooh, Ameya,
thank you."

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.680
Ameya is a lovely woman.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.560
Very focused,
hard working, consistent.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.040
The first time I met her
she was so approachable.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.200
Very good customer service.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.600
The outfit
is very well-fitted.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.200
Excellent.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.000
On point.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.400
She took her time.
Did a very beautiful job.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.480
When I wake up
in the morning,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.280
I know
I have a place to go to.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.920
I will jump out of my bed,
I will run

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.840
like as if I'm going
to get a job in the office.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.760
Even if I'm sick,
I'm always there.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.040
I worked from home before.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.240
When I said
I'm going to move my shop

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.840
to Edmonton Green
Shopping Mall,

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.440
my family was scared.
I said, "I will do it."

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.600
And by God's grace,
I started doing it

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.080
and the moment
everybody is telling me

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.440
I can't do it,
I keep doing it more.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.960
So that is exactly
what put me

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.000
to where I am today.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.600
My name is Marcia.
I am a hairdresser.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.320
I have a passion for hair.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.560
When I decided to do this

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.920
it was like...
I like to create stuff

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.960
and I like
to make people happy.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.440
I like to see a smile
on people's face,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.120
so I know
when I was quite younger,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:14.000
I used to just play around
doing hair just for fun

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.720
and people
were really amazed.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.840
Then I said maybe
I could just

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.440
use this as a profession

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.960
and it started from there.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.280
My shop is
called Marcia's Salon

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.560
Just for people to recognise
it's Marcia.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.920
I was going to use
Fabulous Hair, but no,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.000
but no, Marcia.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.520
People would know
exactly where we at.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.960
The energy here,
some people come in

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.080
and said, "Oh, you're
always having a party!"

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.760
So that made me have
that vibey energy.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.360
Me and my client,

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.680
we talk about
practically everything,

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.000
like relationship,
our lifestyle, men.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.040
Practically every week
there's drama.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.640
Drama being fun, laughter.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.880
Somebody coming in

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.440
with something that just like,

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.880
you just have to just laugh.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.240
You have to just
shake your head and laugh.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.200
Every day is laughter
in my salon.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.560
My name is Christine Oculi.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.560
Our shop is called
Tony's Quality Butchers

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.440
because the meat is fresh.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.160
Tony is an honour.
He's my son.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.400
We name the shop
Tony's Quality Butchers

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.480
because Tony
had a butcher in Brixton,

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.880
so we thought it best
to keep the same name.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.360
Tony is a very nice son.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.600
Very polite,
very hard working.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.200
James, my husband,

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.960
he's the best husband
anybody can ever wish for.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.680
I wanted to become
a market trader

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.960
because I wanted to provide
for the whole community.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.960
The food that people buy
from the shop

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.000
connects them to their
country, to their home.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.000
Because when they come
to buy they will say,

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.680
"Oh, this is here also.
We got this in our country."

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.000
Sometimes we're playing
music and then, you know,

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.720
they are dancing
and then we also, you know,

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.080
join in and dance with them.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.200
We crack jokes. We laugh.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.480
Somebody might come
not very happy,

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.640
but by the time they leave
the shop, we talk to them,

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.360
and they go home laughing.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.640
My name
is Rackel Ewan-Boulyn.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.880
We sell a variety of stuff.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.520
African-Caribbean stuff.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.440
Things from, basically,
all over the world.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:12.000
We have sugar cane,
sometimes watermelons,

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.200
all type of fruits,

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.080
yellow yam from Jamaica,
sweet potato.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.920
We have Uganda sweet potato,
the puna yam,

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.480
and we have things connected
to a lot of countries,

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:23.800
a lot of cultures.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.080
The food we sell

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.200
gives people
a feeling of being home.

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.320
When they're cooking
their food,

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.240
it reminds them that,
basically,

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.000
they're getting
a part of their culture.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.080
Bertha is my mum.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.000
-She's my auntie.
-She's my mum.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.760
She's very determined
and hard-working.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.160
When I think about my mum

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.480
is that
she's a wonderful person.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.960
She is always kind
and helpful

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:47.040
even when somebody is sad,
she always cheers people up.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.280
She's a good team leader,

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.240
she's also like a great,
great mum to me as well.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.840
This job is not easy.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.800
Being on your toes all day,

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:56.200
you have to keep
moving about,

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:58.360
always getting things
to stock up.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.040
But in my case,
it's not hard

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.120
because I have help.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.200
The workers
and the customers,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.480
they are the best.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:07.360
When they come

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.080
and they will tell you
a story

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.440
or they will run a joke
about something

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.920
or they just make your day.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.720
The way
they talk to you is like,

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.000
some of the times
they don't want to leave.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.960
My name is Fatou Inniss.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.080
I've been working here
for one year now.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.880
Dalston is a place
you can get a lot of things.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.040
Mostly stuff from back home,
Africa, and Caribbean.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.560
If you want something
from back home,

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.760
you can find what you need.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.200
I'm selling
African products,

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.000
there're a few from Dubai,
and Caribbean food as well.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.360
I got palm oil
from back home.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.360
Awuchere, chagre.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.160
My customer come and buy
their own country fruit.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:51.520
You can see them,
their face.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.840
they're so happy
when they're buying it.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.400
When they come,
they're always happy.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.520
Yes, please. Yes, please.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:07.360
Being a female trader
in the market,

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:11.760
there are a few of us here.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.600
Mostly men,
but it makes us special.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.560
For me, I think
I can be equal as a man.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:23.280
I look at equality,
person that can do the job,

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:24.680
so there's no difference

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.800
in a man or a woman
being a head of anything,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.960
a company or business.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.920
Can do it as a woman
as well as equal as a man.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.600
Sometimes,
people look down at you

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.880
because it's like
it's not your role.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.880
Well, at the beginning
it was not easy.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.440
I have to get up
every morning and go work.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.320
I'm hard worker.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.720
I don't like
to depend with anyone.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.280
I don't want to wait
for somebody

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:51.280
to come
and put food on my table

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.520
or to come
and put money in my hand.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:54.320
I've been told I'm arrogant.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.120
I've been told,
"You think you're all that."

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.160
And I've been told,
"You're a woman."

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.120
But, to me,

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.480
if you're strong
at something

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.880
and you like it
and you wanna do it,

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.960
I believe
that you should go for it,

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:09.520
whether you're man or woman.

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:14.600
I love my job.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:19.160
The vibe of the people,
the music, the shouting.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:24.000
Chocho, christophene.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.400
You put in a soup.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.600
You cook it done
with saltfish.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:30.720
People are friendly.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.960
Even though we don't know
each other that much,

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.320
but when you pass each other
we just say hello.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:38.520
Doesn't matter
what colour you are,

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.920
English, Black.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.200
-Get characters in Dalston.
-Innit.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:45.040
You put it in your mouth
and your wiggly it around.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.520
There's some things that
you only see in Dalston.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.280
D'you know what I mean?

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.880
It's really loving here.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.120
We have lovely people,
different character,

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.720
and different background.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.320
I just love seeing people
you know, walking around,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.440
talking,
different languages.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.720
The Indian men,
they can speak everything.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:05.520
Jamaican, they have little
African accents, everything.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.960
It's Dalston,
it's multi-cultured.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.200
Like you might hear
the Indian man

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.440
telling you "wagwan", so…

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.760
I was born in Lagos,
Nigeria.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.280
I am from Jamaica.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.080
I'm from Gambia.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:19.080
Growing up in Jamaica
is awesome.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.400
It's like
the best place to be.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:21.720
The food,

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:24.560
the vibes of the people,
the parties.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.640
A lot of the market
reminds me of Jamaica.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.160
The clothes stalls,
the food stalls,

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.600
the shouting of the products
that we are selling,

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.800
the music.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.360
I think that the ingredients
people buy from our shop

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:36.800
connects them
to their country.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.920
It gives people
a sense of home.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.720
Dalston always reminds me
of Ghana.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.840
Everything around here
in the market

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.520
reminds me of home, Nigeria.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.720
-Uganda.
-Jamaica.

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.240
-Gambia.
-West Africa.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.640
And the people themselves,
they remind me of home.

